Subject: Optimize-Chunk-Ticket-Management

Author: VeltisMC Development Team
Date: 2026-06-19

Reason:
Vanilla chunk ticket management uses suboptimal data structures for
tracking chunk loading priorities, causing unnecessary overhead during
high-traffic chunk loading scenarios (e.g., player teleportation, world
exploration). The default ticket propagation algorithm does not scale
well with multiple players loading distinct regions simultaneously.

Impact:
Reduces chunk load latency under high concurrency. Improves server
responsiveness during player teleportation and world exploration.
Lowers CPU usage from ticket sorting and distance calculations.

Migration Note:
This patch modifies net.minecraft.server.level.TicketManager and
net.minecraft.server.level.ChunkMap to use Moonrise's optimized
chunk ticket tracking. Requires VeltisPlatformHooks to be active.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/level/TicketManager.java b/net/minecraft/server/level/TicketManager.java
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/level/TicketManager.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/level/TicketManager.java
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+// VeltisMC: Moonrise chunk ticket management
+// Replaces vanilla TicketManager sorting with Moonrise's priority-queue
+// based ticket dispatcher. See ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.patches.chunk_system
+// for the actual implementation (via mixins).
+//
+// This patch simply enables the Moonrise chunk system hooks by ensuring
+// VeltisPlatformHooks is loaded before any TicketManager operations.
+// The actual algorithm change is performed by moonrise.mixins.json mixins:
+//   - chunk_system.TicketMixin
+//   - chunk_system.TicketStorageMixin
+//   - chunk_system.TicketTypeMixin
+//   - chunk_system.ChunkMap$DistanceManagerMixin
